    "done_when": "Lead ruling: fix the clear errors, then re-measure; the fixes are on main: clip-vertex tangent 3825858f2, boundary-flux derivative 38465cf46, first-moment centroid row with derived tolerance 45f5ee8ef (decision centroid-row-definition). On main, run the weak-rotation-reactor-static -110 unit-leverage positive control at 135 cells through benchmarks/centroid_constrained_fixture_receipt.py as ONE H200 job (betelgeuse, reservation gpu_0003_grpA, one card, explicit --mem, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter without uv, RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch), passing clip_mode='exact' explicitly on the request and confirming the receipt records exact as the mode in force; inputs unchanged from H200 job 1280380 otherwise. The receipt, under docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/repaired-remeasure/, records per Newton pass the global residual, the first-moment row residual against its derived tolerance, the compensating field amplitudes and the gauge-free span offset against the 1e-3-of-span clause net of the compensator's closed-form flux. Draw line-contour panels of the terminal state beside the analytic reference on shared levels, with both null sets and the wall, per the AGENTS.md plotting rules. The report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-repaired-constrained-remeasure.md compares every number with job 1280380 (field -2.1256e-2 T, span offset 8.3e-2 of span, wall flux -4.5 to -20.6 Wb) and states plainly whether the converged map now matches the analytic one. No solver source change in this node. A baseline arm, if any, extracts only the subtrees it imports and removes them before the manifest. Commit the receipt and write the manifest before waiting on the job.",
